case: undertow-jboss-wildfly-web-server-cve-2018-1067
pair: CVE-2016-4993 (V1=TARGET, incomplete)  ->  CVE-2018-1067 (V2 fix)
class: HTTP response splitting / CRLF header injection (CWE-113)
sink:  io.undertow.server.protocol.http.HttpResponseConduit.writeString

REBUILD (2026-07-16): moved from BANNED in-process trigger (compose exec + in-container
127.0.0.1 socket) to a REAL, EXTERNALLY-triggered Undertow HTTP server, mirroring
cases/netty-cve-2020-7238 and cases/haproxy-cve-2023-40225.
  - ReflectServer.java now binds 0.0.0.0:8080 (was 127.0.0.1) and is PUBLISHED to a host port.
  - docker-compose.yml publishes v0=39733, v1=39734, v2=39735.
  - oracle.py runs on the HOST: socket.create_connection((127.0.0.1, <port>)) sends a raw
    GET /reflect?v=... whose reflected value carries the CRLF payload, reads the raw response
    bytes, and STRICT-parses for a genuine standalone CRLF-framed "X-Split" header.
  - No docker compose exec; no in-container python. attack.py is now UNUSED/stale.

